SCALE PROBES (product host — `/tmp/s710_peer2_1095493`)
---

Hang budget = **10s** (`timeout`). Dual-repro where noted.
Fixtures ephemeral; not committed.

### Unused SECRET name (`// SECRET: A×L` + `println(1)`)
Exercises `c_parse_secret_env` only (name is not an IDENT in the body;
lexer treats the directive as a comment).

| L | emit-c (10s) | rss | rc |
|---|--------------|-----|----|
| 8 | **0.06s** | — | 0 |
| 256 | **0.13–0.20s** dual | ~7 MB | 0 |
| 512 | **0.30–0.32s** dual | — | 0 |
| 1024 | **0.97–1.15s** dual | ~15 MB | 0 |

**No hang. No SIGTERM/124.**

### Fail rail (directive parsed + sink refuse)
| Probe | Result |
|-------|--------|
| L=256 `println(A×256)` | rc=1 `ERR	secret	println sink refuses SECRET A…` **0.11–0.19s** dual **PASS** |
| L=1024 `println(A×1024)` | rc=1 same refuse class **1.09–1.45s** **PASS** |

### Isolation
| Probe | emit-c | Note |
|-------|--------|------|
| `// A×1024` (no SECRET) | **0.29s** | file walk / comment only |
| `// NOTE: A×1024` | **0.32s** | same class |
| `// SECRET: tok` + `// A×1024` | **0.13s** | short name parse |
| `tokens` on SECRET L=1024 unused | **0.02s** | lexer skips comment |

SECRET L=1024 unused (~1.0s) vs comment L=1024 (~0.3s) is the parse-env
ident walk + **host-side per-char concat**. Still **≪10s**. After a
rebuild, this delta should shrink; this peer did **not** rebuild to
prove that.

